\title{Binomial trees and binomial coefficients}
\date{2026-11-21T19:28:23Z}
\tag{algorithms}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\taxon{Remark}
\p{Binomial trees are called \em{binomial} since a binomial tree of order #{n} has #{\binom n k} nodes at depth #{k}. This can also be proved by induction, using some facts about [binomial coefficients](00GH) (just think about adding a row of [Pascal’s triangle](00GL) shifted against itself to get the next row).}
